IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `lta-types`
IMPORT `lta-repair`

-- Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK) — GOAL 2: SERVICE CHARGES (ss 18-20B,
-- 21B).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1985-70.txt.

§ `Goal 2 — service charges`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- s 20B(1) "If any of the relevant costs taken into account in determining
-- the amount of any service charge were incurred more than 18 months before a
-- demand for payment of the service charge is served on the tenant, then
-- (subject to subsection (2)), the tenant shall not be liable to pay so much
-- of the service charge as reflects the costs so incurred." (2) "Subsection
-- (1) shall not apply if, within the period of 18 months beginning with the
-- date when the relevant costs in question were incurred, the tenant was
-- notified in writing that those costs had been incurred and that he would
-- subsequently be required ... to contribute to them".
@ref s 20B
GIVEN i IS A `Cost item`, served IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20B bars the item` i `in a demand served on` served IF
        served GREATER THAN eighteenMonths
    AND NOT notified
    WHERE
        eighteenMonths MEANS `the last day of the` 18 `months beginning with` (i's `incurred on`)
        notified MEANS
            CONSIDER i's `tenant notified on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST n  THEN n AT MOST eighteenMonths

-- s 19(1): costs count "only to the extent that they are reasonably incurred,
-- and ... only if the services or works are of a reasonable standard". s 20(1),
-- (7): without consultation (or dispensation), the contribution of a tenant
-- whose contribution would exceed the appropriate amount is limited to it.
@ref ss 19(1), 20(1), (7), 20B
@export The amount of one item of relevant costs a tenant is liable to pay in a service charge under the Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK): nothing if it was incurred more than 18 months before the demand without written notice within those 18 months (s 20B); otherwise the part reasonably incurred (s 19), limited to the appropriate amount for qualifying works without consultation or dispensation (s 20). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN i IS A `Cost item`  @desc The amount charged, the part reasonably incurred, when it was incurred and notified, and whether s 20 consultation applied and failed
      served IS A DATE    @desc The day the demand was served
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payable part of` i `in a demand served on` served MEANS
    IF   `s 20B bars the item` i `in a demand served on` served
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF   i's `qualifying works without consultation`
         THEN `the lesser of` reasonable (i's `the appropriate amount`)
         ELSE reasonable
    WHERE
        reasonable MEANS `the lesser of` (i's `amount charged`) (i's `amount reasonably incurred`)

@ref ss 19, 20, 20B
@export The total service charge a tenant is liable to pay on a demand under the Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK): the sum over the items of relevant costs of the part payable after ss 19, 20 and 20B. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN d IS A `Service charge demand`  @desc The day the demand was served and its items of relevant costs
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the service charge payable on` d MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD `the payable part of` i `in a demand served on` (d's `served on`)) (d's `items`))

-- s 21B(1) "A demand for the payment of a service charge must be accompanied
-- by a summary of the rights and obligations of tenants of dwellings in
-- relation to service charges." (3) "A tenant may withhold payment of a
-- service charge which has been demanded from him if subsection (1) is not
-- complied with in relation to the demand."
@ref s 21B(1), (3)
@export Whether a tenant may withhold payment of a service charge demand under s 21B of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK): the demand was not accompanied by the summary of tenants' rights and obligations. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN d IS A `Service charge demand`  @desc Whether the demand was accompanied by the summary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant may withhold payment of` d IF
    NOT (d's `accompanied by the summary of rights and obligations`)
